# Cejas Internacionales Rules

Read `AGENTS.md` first. It is the shared rule source for Codex, Cursor, Claude Code, and other coding agents.

For implementation, follow `docs/cliente/implementacion-fases/README.md` and update the relevant phase checklist instead of working from memory.

Critical rules:

- Do not touch `main` unless Jeffrey explicitly says so.
- Use `develop` by default.
- Do not edit generated artifacts as source.
- V1 is informative only: no store, checkout, cart, booking form, or admin.
- Main CTA is `Contacta conmigo`.
- Reservation/contact is WhatsApp only.
- Colombia WhatsApp: `573167742299`.
- Spain/Europe/Switzerland WhatsApp: `34603804837`.
- Physical/legal address only Cali, Colombia.
- Do not invent Spain or Switzerland offices.
- Do not mix services between markets.
- Public website must be bilingual: Spanish and international English.
- Add Spanish and English content together for every new public page/component/metadata/CTA/schema/alt text.
- SEO starts from architecture: crawlable HTML, clean URLs, metadata, schema, sitemap, robots, hreflang and Core Web Vitals.
- QA follows `docs/cliente/implementacion-fases/QA-SENIOR-MATRIZ-PRUEBAS-WEB.md`: smoke, regression, E2E, visual regression, WAVE/axe, Lighthouse, links, i18n and security headers.
- GA4 requires cookie banner, cookie policy and Consent Mode; do not load analytics before analytics consent.
- Legal notice, privacy and cookies pages are required in Spanish and English.
- Palette: palo de rosa `#B76E79`, white, black. Use semantic tokens, no raw hex in components.
- Typography: Marcellus headings, Manrope body/UI.
- Buttons use natural width by default; no full-width card CTAs unless justified.
- Hover must have focus/tap/click equivalents.
- No generic AI UI: no nested cards, no orbs/blobs, no gradient text, no endless identical card grids, no carousel as primary content.
- Future DB/admin is Supabase; V1 uses typed local data and query functions.
- If running localhost, use `3000` if free, otherwise next available port and report the URL.
- Git push/fetch: non-interactive only — `GIT_ACCESS_TOKEN` from `.env.local` or `npm run git:push` (see `.cursor/rules/git-github-noninteractive.mdc`).
